  "model": "Sol I Blinder",
  "category": "strobe_or_blinder",
  "description": "Elation SOL I Blinder is a single-head strobe-style blinder with one round LED array, mounted on a U-shaped yoke bracket that sits on a base plate; the housing is a cylinder roughly 0.26 m wide, 0.27 m deep and 0.17 m tall, assuming the mesh units are centimetres. The base is the ARM mesh, a U-yoke about 26 by 21 by 11 units with two side arms carrying the head, and the base plate probably has two round feet or knobs that are not separate nodes. The head is a single can hanging between the yoke arms, with a flat lens disc at its front and a square-grid wire guard across the face. Pan rotates the whole yoke assembly about the vertical axis, and tilt rotates the head about the arm pivot, both manually aimed with a range of about 360 degrees per the tree, though the physical limits are unconfirmed. The front emitter is one circular diffuser panel, not individually resolvable pixels, so there is one controllable cell. A black clamp knob sits on the side at the tilt pivot.",
